ubmitting is dominated causally — it's a stag-hunt style game, not PD. EDT with correlation: cooperate (pass) if correlation high enough. ρ = P(other submits | I submit) ≈ P(other passes | I pass) for identical copies. V(pass)=2ρ+5(1-ρ)=5-3ρ; V(submit)=4ρ+0(1-ρ)=4ρ. Pass better iff 5-3ρ > 4ρ iff ρ < 5/7 ≈ 0.714. Identical LLM copies with same essay: correlation very high, ρ→1. Then submit gives 4 < pass 2... wait at ρ=1: pass=2, submit=4. So submit better under EDT with near-perfect correlation. Interesting—unlike twin PD, here defect (submit) is the correlated-optimal action at high ρ. Since copies run same reasoning, ρ≈1, submit yields 4 vs pass 2. So submit.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5716,"completion_tokens":405,"total_tokens":6121,"cost":0.00099846,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":512,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00099846,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00079596,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0002025},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":272,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}